   220	## 4. Radius-two branch-B face
   220	## 4. Radius-two branch-B face
   221	
   222	This section is conditional on the banked premise that p.209's printed
   223	`x^15y^40+...` is the radius-two `T_3` leader.  Moh's ellipsis alone does not
   224	prove that identification; Xu's further expansion supplies the same datum.
   225	
   226	Translate the double root to zero and retain `a != 0`:
   227	
   228	```text
   229	H=z^2(z+3a),
   230	R=H^12 q,          q=z^4+q3*z^3+q2*z^2+q1*z+q0.
   231	```
   232	
   233	The necessary leader equation is
   234	
   235	```text
   236	2 H R_z - 25 H_z R = k H^14,
   237	```
   238	
   239	or, after division by `H^12`,
   240	
   241	```text
   242	2 H q_z - H_z q - k H^2 = 0.                           (4.1)
   243	```
   244	
   245	The declared ring is
   246	
   247	```text
   248	Q[T,q0,q1,q2,q3,k,a], lex,  T*a*k-1=0.                 (4.2)
   249	```
   250	
   251	There are six unknowns excluding the wrapper and six raw nonzero coefficient
   252	rows; the last is `2a` times the preceding row, hence five independent rows.
   253	The exact reduced basis of (4.1)--(4.2) is
   254	
   255	```text
   256	5*T*a-1,
   257	q0,
   258	18*a^3+q1,
   259	3*a^2+q2,
   260	-4*a+q3,
   261	k-5.
   262	```
   263	
   264	It is nonunit and one-dimensional.  The wrapper-only and unsaturated ideals
   265	are also nonunit; adjoining `a` or adjoining `k` makes the wrapped ideal the
   266	unit ideal.  Therefore
   267	
   268	```text
   269	q=z(z-2a)(z+3a)^2,
   270	R=z^25(z+3a)^14(z-2a).                                  (4.3)
   271	```
   272	
   273	With `z=xy`, the bivariate faces are
   274	
   275	```text
   276	F_2  = y^12(xy+3a)^6,
   277	G_2  = y^18(xy+3a)^9,
   278	T2_2 = y^10(xy+3a)^5,
   279	T3_2 = y^25(xy+3a)^14(xy-2a).
   280	```
   281	
   282	Direct symbolic differentiation, rather than an ODE inference, gives
   283	
   284	```text
   285	J(F_2,G_2)=0,
   286	J(T3_2,G_2)=45*x*y^44*(xy+3a)^22.                       (4.4)
   287	```
   288	
   289	The maximum original-coordinate degrees from the termwise inverse test (2.2)
   290	are respectively `66,99,55,145`.  Equations (4.3)--(4.4) certify
   291	`SURVIVES[PRINTED-LEADER-ODE-FACE]` only, under that premise.
   292	
   293	## 5. Jacobian lift by descending bands
   294	
   295	This section works in the explicitly typed slice
   296	
   297	```text
   298	SLICE[Omega_0: X=x^-1, Y=x^3 y; z=xy; fixed top and radius-two faces].
   299	```
   300	
   301	Normalize
   302	
   303	```text
   304	Omega_0(F)=x^-12 f(x,z),       f=sum_(n>=0) x^n f_n(z),
   305	Omega_0(G)=x^-18 g(x,z),       g=sum_(n>=0) x^n g_n(z),
   306	f_0=H^6,                       g_0=H^9.
   307	```
   308	
   309	Because `J_(x,y)=x J_(x,z)`, the full transformed Jacobian equation is exactly
   310	
   311	```text
   312	18 f_z g - 12 f g_z + x(f_x g_z-f_z g_x) = c*x^31.     (5.1)
   313	```
   314	
   315	At band `n`, let
   316	
   317	```text
   318	E_n=sum_(r+s=n) ((18-s) f_r' g_s + (r-12) f_r g_s')
   319	        - c*[n=31].                                    (5.2)
   320	```
   321	
   322	Here a prime in (5.2) means `d/dz`.  With
   323	
   324	```text
   325	q_n=3H^3 f_n-2g_n,
   326	L_n(q)=2H q' + (n-18)H' q,
   327	```
   328	
   329	the new-variable part is the checked factorization
   330	
   331	```text
   332	E_n(new)=3H^5 L_n(q_n).                                (5.3)
   333	```
   334	
   335	This exposes constant pivots before any nonlinear elimination.  Dimension
   336	convention: fix one arbitrary nonzero target value of `c` and do not count it;
   337	the table adds `a` to the coefficient fibre.  The truncated ambient ideal with
   338	`c` left variable has every listed total increased by one.  The band ledger is:
   339	
   340	| band | new unknowns `F+G` | raw / quotient rows | new rank | old compatibility rows | dimension incl. `a`, fixed `c` | result |
   341	|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
   342	| 0 | 0 | 0 / 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | face fixed |
   343	| 1 | `17+26=43` | 32 / 27 | 26 | 0 | 18 | consistent |
   344	| 2 | `16+25=41` | 36, then 30 / 25 | 24 | 5 | 30 | consistent |
   345	| 3 | `15+24=39` | 30 / 25 | 24 | 4 | 41 | consistent |
   346	| 4 | `14+23=37` | 29 / 24 | 22 | 5 | 51 | consistent |
   347	| 5 | `13+22=35` | 28 / 23 after compatibility | 22 | codimension 5 | 59 | consistent; 15 components |
   348	| 6 | `12+21=33` | 27 / 22 | 20 | 17 remainder rows | not asserted | exact next system |
   349	
   350	The scalar first enters an equation at band 31, so these early counts do not
   351	show that the chosen `c != 0` can be realized.
   352	
   353	### Band 1
