   625	## 6. Xu's `delta=5/2` split
   626	
   627	Xu's leading data at `delta=5/2` are
   628	
   629	```text
   630	f(sigma)       = p(pi)^6  t^-3   + ...,
   631	g(sigma)       = p(pi)^9  t^-9/2 + ...,
   632	T2(sigma)      = p(pi)^5  t^-5/2 + ...,
   633	(T3)_f(sigma)  = p(pi)^22 t^-11  + ...,
   634	T3(sigma)      = q(pi)    t^-5   + ...,
   635	deg p=3,       deg q=40.
   636	```
   637	
   638	Put `x=s^2`, `y=pi/s`.  Then
   639	
   640	```text
   641	Omega(P)(s^2,pi/s)
   642	 =P(s^-2,a_0+a_1s^2+a_2s^4+pi*s^5).
   643	```
   644	
   645	Integer `x` exponents force `p^6` to be even in `s`.  For monic
   646	`p=z^3+A z^2+Bz+C`, the nine odd coefficient rows have triangular leading
   647	pivots
   648	
   649	```text
   650	[z^17]p^6=6A,
   651	[z^15]p^6 |_(A=0)=6C.
   652	```
   653	
   654	Hence
   655	
   656	```text
   657	p=z(z^2-rho),        rho != 0,        disc(p)=4rho^3.  (6.1)
   658	```
   659	
   660	The parity saturation is explicit.  In `Q[U,A,C,B]` with lex order, add
   661	`UB-1`.  The wrapped reduced basis is `{UB-1,A,C}`; the wrapper-only and raw
   662	parity ideals are nonunit, while adjoining `B` gives `[1]`.  The point
   663	`A=C=0,B=-1,U=-1` is a positive control.  Then set `B=-rho`.
   664	
   665	This separates the levels correctly: at radius two the strict-below common
   666	face is still `z^3`; at radius `5/2` the at-level polynomial is (6.1).  The
   667	three roots describe a `9+9+9` split of cover roots.  The two roots
   668	`+sqrt(rho)` and `-sqrt(rho)` are exchanged by denominator-two conjugacy and
   669	are not thereby proved to be two physical places.
   670	
   671	Xu's factorization `q=p^10 q_1`, `deg q_1=10`, reduces
   672	`p q'-10p'q=kappa*p^14` exactly to
   673	
   674	```text
   675	q_1'=kappa*p^3.
   676	```
   677	
   678	In the monic `T_3` gauge `kappa=10`, and direct integration gives
   679	
   680	```text
   681	q_1=z^10-(15/4)rho*z^8+5rho^2*z^6-(5/2)rho^3*z^4+b_0. (6.2)
   682	```
   683	
   684	Xu's displayed `kappa=-2` is a scalar-equivalent normalization.  In the exact
   685	ring
   686	
   687	```text
   688	Q[T,b1,...,b9,kappa,b0,rho], lex,  T*rho*kappa-1=0,
   689	```
   690	
   691	there are 12 unknowns excluding the wrapper and ten effective coefficient
   692	rows.  The reduced component is
   693	
   694	```text
   695	b1,b2,b3, 2b4+5rho^3, b5, b6-5rho^2, b7,
   696	4b8+15rho, b9, kappa-10.
   697	```
   698	
   699	It has dimension two, with parameters `(rho,b_0)`.  The wrapped ideal is
   700	nonunit; adjoining `rho` or `kappa` gives `[1]`, and
   701	`rho=b_0=1,kappa=10,T=1/10` is a positive witness.
   702	Moreover,
   703	
   704	```text
   705	Res_z(p,q_1)=b_0(4b_0-rho^5)^2/16.
   706	```
   707	
   708	Thus the same witness lies on the optional coprime open; coprimality is not
   709	needed merely for face survival.
   710	
