   149	## Next-level setup
   150	
   151	In original monic source coordinates, with `x=t^-1`, the `delta=5/2`
   152	principal-minor expansion has the form
   153	
   154	```text
   155	sigma = a_-1 t^-1 + a_0 + a_1 t + a_2 t^2 + pi t^(5/2).
   156	```
   157	
   158	The tower fixes the principal minor direction and multiplicity data.  After a
   159	linear normalization of the two top directions, the degree-11 common
   160	approximate-root leader has top form `Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8`; the chosen minor line
   161	is the multiplicity-3 direction.  The data force the face multiplicities
   162	
   163	```text
   164	g: 27,   f: 18,   T2: 15,   (T3)_f: 66,
   165	```
   166	
   167	and the displayed powers `p^9,p^6,p^5,p^22`.  They do not determine
   168	`a_0,a_1,a_2`, nor the full lower coefficients of `f,g,T2,T3`.  A fail-closed
   169	original-coordinate system would need the coefficient arrays for
   170	
   171	```text
   172	h = y^11 + lower terms,       h(sigma)=p t^-1/2 + ...
   173	f = h^6 + sum_{i=1}^6 alpha_i h^(6-i),
   174	g = h^9 + sum_{i=2}^9 beta_i h^(9-i),
   175	T2 = h^5 + lower h-adic terms,
   176	T3 with local quotient T3/h^10 = q1 + ...
   177	```
   178	
   179	plus the effective quasi-approximate-root recurrences in `K[f,g]` and the
   180	original `J(f,g)=1` equations.  Xu does not print those equations.
   181	
   182	For the bounded prolongation I used the straightened local chart
   183	
   184	```text
   185	s^2=t,        x=s^-2,        y=pi*s^5,
   186	h = p/s + A0(pi) + A1(pi)s + A2(pi)s^2 + ...
   187	Q = q1(pi) + B1(pi)s + B2(pi)s^2 + ...
   188	```
   189	
   190	and imposed
   191	
   192	```text
   193	D_s(Q,h)+2*s^2*h^4 = 0.
   194	```
   195	
   196	The `h` supports are not arbitrary: a monomial `x^i y^j` of a degree-11
   197	polynomial contributes to `[s^r]h` only when `5j-2i=r` and `i+j<=11`.
   198	Through the computed orders this gives
   199	
   200	```text
   201	r=0: pi^0,pi^2
   202	r=1: pi^1,pi^3
   203	r=2: pi^2
   204	r=3: pi^1,pi^3
   205	r=4: pi^2
   206	r=5: pi^1,pi^3
   207	```
   208	
   209	The `Q` coefficients were allowed up to degree 18 at each new order.  This is
   210	a local necessary/superset computation: inconsistency would be meaningful, but
   211	consistency is only a counting bound because it does not enforce the full
   212	`T3 in K[f,g]` bridge or all original polynomiality correlations.
   213	
   214	The first two omitted equations can be written compactly before solving.  Put
   215	`p=pi(pi^2-c)`, `h=p/s+A0+A1*s+...`, and `Q=q1+B1*s+B2*s^2+...`.  The
   216	coefficient of `s^-1` in `D_s(Q,h)+2*s^2*h^4` is
   217	
   218	```text
   219	(p B1)' + 8 p^3 A0 = 0.
   220	```
   221	
   222	With the degree-11 straightened `h` support, `A0=u0+u2*pi^2`.  Polynomiality of
   223	`B1` forces `u0=-(c/3)u2`; in the driver's free-parameter coordinate this is
   224	
   225	```text
   226	A0 = (b1_9*c)/2 - (3*b1_9/2) pi^2.
   227	```
   228	
   229	The coefficient of `s^0` is
   230	
   231	```text
   232	p B2' + 2p' B2 + 10p^3 A1 + 12p^2 A0^2 + B1 A0' = 0.
   233	```
   234	
   235	The straightened support gives `A1=v1*pi+v3*pi^3`.  After substituting the
   236	first-order solution, the exact solve leaves one new free parameter `b2_8`:
   237	
   238	```text
   239	A1 = ((3*b1_9^2 - 2*b2_8)/10) pi
   240	   + (2*(9*b1_9^2 + 4*b2_8)/(15*c)) pi^3.
   241	```
   242	
   243	Thus the requested next two omitted orders are not merely "not contradicted";
   244	they have an explicit localized polynomial solution branch over `Q[c,c^-1]`.
   245	
   246	## Computation
   247	
   248	Wrapper controls in `Q[c,T]` passed:
   249	
   250	```text
   251	ideal(c,T*c-1)       -> unit ideal
   252	ideal(c-1,T*c-1)     -> non-unit ideal
   253	```
   254	
   255	Controls reproducing Xu's exclusions:
   256	
   257	* `delta=2`, `[1,1,1]`: equation
   258	  `2p q' - 25p' q = k p^14`.  Since `c != 0`, `p=pi(pi^2-c)` is squarefree.
   259	  At each simple root of `p`, if `q` has multiplicity `r`, the left side has
   260	  multiplicity `r` because `2r-25 != 0`; the right side has multiplicity 14.
   261	  Thus `r=14` at all three roots, so `deg q>=42`, contradicting Xu's
   262	  `deg q=40`.  Verdict: `EXCLUDED`.
   263	* `delta=7/3`: after Xu's non-exceptional reduction
   264	  `q=p^13(pi-d)`, the reduced polynomial is
   265	  `k*c*pi - k*pi^3 + 12*c*d - 21*c*pi - 36*d*pi^2 + 45*pi^3`.
   266	  Saturating by `c != 0` with `T*c-1` gives Groebner basis `[1]`.
   267	  Verdict: `EXCLUDED`.
   268	
   269	The `delta=5/2` local lift stayed consistent through `s^4`, i.e. through six
   270	coefficient levels including the leading `s^-2` reduced equation and the
   271	omitted levels `s^-1,s^0,s^1,s^2,s^3,s^4`.  The requested "next two orders"
   272	are `s^-1` and `s^0`; both are consistent.
   273	
   274	The order records from `xu52_reduced_lift.json` are:
   275	
   276	```text
   277	s^-1: 21 equations, 21 new variables, 20 solved, free b1_9
   278	      a0_0 = b1_9*c/2
   279	      a0_2 = -3*b1_9/2
   280	s^0 : 21 equations, 21 new variables, 20 solved, free b2_8
   281	      a1_1 = (3*b1_9^2 - 2*b2_8)/10
   282	      a1_3 = 2*(9*b1_9^2 + 4*b2_8)/(15*c)
   283	s^1 : 21 equations, 20 new variables, 20 solved, no new free parameter
   284	      a2_2 = -b1_9*(3*b1_9^2 + b2_8)/(2*c)
   285	s^2 : 21 equations, 21 new variables, 20 solved, free b4_8
   286	s^3 : 21 equations, 20 new variables, 20 solved, no new free parameter
   287	s^4 : 21 equations, 21 new variables, 20 solved, free b6_8
   288	```
   289	
   290	Every emitted coefficient was rechecked symbolically after substitution.
   291	Denominators are rational constants and powers of `c`; the computation is on
   292	the localized component `c != 0`.
   293	
   294	Dimension count:
   295	
   296	```text
   297	through next two orders s^-1,s^0:  c plus b1_9,b2_8  -> dimension 3 localized
   298	through s^4:                       c plus b1_9,b2_8,b4_8,b6_8
   299	                                  -> dimension 5 localized
   300	after the slice c=1:               dimension 4 through s^4
