   513	## 7. What the exact full system would require
   514	
   515	There is a finite first-principles system, but it is not Moh's missing
   516	11-variable system.  Start with the 7326 old-coordinate coefficients in the
   517	two monic total-degree arrays and parameters `a_0,a_1,a_2`.  Form `F,G` by
   518	(3.1); impose all inverse polynomiality relations from (3.2), both Newton
   519	faces, the universal approximate-root definitions of `T_2^psi,T_3^psi`, and
   520	every coefficient of
   521	
   522	```text
   523	J(F,G)+c*x=0, c!=0, T*c-1=0
   524	```
   525	
   526	(with the sign convention above).  One must then prove and apply the
   527	filtration-preserving h-adic/gauge eliminations that map this system to eleven
   528	variables.  Pp.209--210 omit precisely those eliminations and the resulting
   529	support.  Saturating an invented eleven-monomial slice would not answer the
   530	question.
   531	
   532	Under the declared `T_3`-leader premise, the reduced ODE systems are exact
   533	necessary images of the full Jacobian system.  Their logical force is then
   534	asymmetric: emptiness of C lifts to the full fixed-radius-two C coefficient
   535	branch, while nonemptiness of B does not lift backward without solving all
   536	omitted coefficient equations.  Without that premise, both statements are
   537	only about the conditional ODE systems.
   538	
   539	There is a second exhaustiveness gap.  P.209 asserts the radius-two description
   540	but does not prove that principal minor roots cannot first split at another
   541	admissible radius.  As an external supplement, Yansong Xu, *Intersection
   542	Numbers and Split of Minor Roots*,
   543	[arXiv:1604.07683v4](https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.07683), Section 8, supplies the
   544	radius-two `T_3` data and proves the three-root exclusion, but also records a
   545	possible `delta=5/2` split and describes `(99,66)` as open.  This is
   546	`EXTERNAL-SUPPLEMENT`, not part of the frozen-source proof.
