   152	Thus the Laurent tail at later bands is fixed by the binomial in (2.7); it is
   153	not a new coefficient.  The mechanically enumerated spaces are:
   154	
   155	| object | `(D,L,m)` | non-strict dimension | strict fixed-face kernel |
   156	|---|---|---:|---:|
   157	| `F` | `(66,12,-2)` | 181 | 146 |
   158	| `G` | `(99,18,-3)` | 388 | 336 |
   159	| `T_2` | `(55,10,-5/3)` | 129 | 100 |
   160	| `T_3` | `(145,25,-5)` | 816 | 740 |
   161	
   162	These are exact old-polynomial counts for the two declared inequalities in
   163	the stated slice, not the full source filtration and not Moh's 11.  The `F`
   164	strict generators start in bands 1 through 15 with counts
   165	
   166	```text
   167	17,16,15,14,13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,4,3,1,
   168	```
   169	
   170	and the `G` generators start in bands 1 through 23 with counts
   171	
   172	```text
   173	26,25,24,23,22,21,20,19,18,17,16,15,14,13,12,11,
   174	10,9,7,6,4,3,1.
   175	```
   176	
   177	This is a bounded necessary slice in place of a blind 7,326-row expansion.
   178	
   179	## 3. Why the zero-jet slice is not the full chart
   180	
   181	It is harmless to remove `a_0` by an old polynomial translation, and `a_2`
   182	can be absorbed into `z` while centring the double root.  The `a_1` term is
   183	different.  Write `u=a_1`.  For the cubic approximate root,
   184	
   185	```text
   186	K=x^11 h(x^-1,w/x),
   187	K|_(x=0)=w^3(w-1)^8,
   188	w=u*x^2+x^3*z.                                         (3.1)
   189	```
   190	
   191	The fixed major face has boundary weight 32, so its strict perturbations obey
   192	`3r+4q>=33` at `w=1`.  Parameterizing this divisibility first leaves 21
   193	coefficients.  Expanding (3.1), killing every term below
   194	`x^9`, and fixing the `x^9` coefficient to
   195	
   196	```text
   197	H=z^2(z+3a)
   198	```
   199	
   200	gives 18 linear equations.  The exact constant-pivot elimination has 18
   201	`Q*` pivots and no residual equation.  Three tail coefficients remain free:
   202	
   203	```text
   204	c_7_4, c_10_1, c_11_0.
   205	```
   206	
   207	Together with `(a,u)` this is a five-dimensional `h` order space.  Every
   208	original row was checked after the resolved triangular substitution, and no
   209	division by `a` or `u` occurred.  In particular, `u` survives symbolically;
   210	these order rows do not license setting `u=0`.  Later `T_2,T_3` or Jacobian
   211	rows could still force it.
   212	
   213	This calculation is only `H-ORDER-SPACE`, not the full lift: it does not
   214	invent the unprinted simultaneous Laurent-field gauge, the `4/9` centre, or
   215	the complete canonical definitions of `T_2^psi,T_3^psi`.  It is nevertheless
   216	a decisive scope check: no source row yet identifies the zero-jet slice with
   217	Moh's full coefficient variety, so its nonemptiness or emptiness cannot be
   218	promoted.
   219	
   220	## 4. Radius-two branch-B face
   221	
   222	This section is conditional on the banked premise that p.209's printed
   223	`x^15y^40+...` is the radius-two `T_3` leader.  Moh's ellipsis alone does not
   224	prove that identification; Xu's further expansion supplies the same datum.
   225	
   226	Translate the double root to zero and retain `a != 0`:
   227	
   228	```text
   229	H=z^2(z+3a),
   230	R=H^12 q,          q=z^4+q3*z^3+q2*z^2+q1*z+q0.
   231	```
   232	
   233	The necessary leader equation is
   234	
   235	```text
   236	2 H R_z - 25 H_z R = k H^14,
   237	```
   238	
   239	or, after division by `H^12`,
   240	
   241	```text
   242	2 H q_z - H_z q - k H^2 = 0.                           (4.1)
   243	```
   244	
   245	The declared ring is
   246	
   247	```text
   248	Q[T,q0,q1,q2,q3,k,a], lex,  T*a*k-1=0.                 (4.2)
   249	```
