     3	Check before promotion.
     4	
     5	- **Flag/place/series.** Never identify a cv flag, physical place, and cover
     6	  series. Separate strict-below from at-level parting and denominator shedding.
     7	- **Per-ray/exit-set charge.** Charge only a typed first-separation set; prove
     8	  flags distinct and count each once.
     9	- **Carrier/attainment.** `REPRESENTATIVE` is not `FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT`. The
    10	  latter aliases `FULL_ACTUAL_FIRST_SEPARATION` and supplies only a floor,
    11	  never attainment.
    12	- **Pole/interior.** Use pole identities only after checking the vertex class
    13	  and every source hypothesis.
    14	- **Floor/attainment.** A lower bound is not exact; equality needs a theorem or
    15	  a witness covering every omitted term.
    16	- **`sat()` wrapping.** Extract the ideal component, assert its ring, and run
    17	  positive and negative controls.
    18	- **Raw remainder degree.** Normal-form in the declared quotient/localization,
    19	  branch on vanished leaders, and handle zero.
    20	- **Variable/ring map.** Declare the map, generator order, coefficient field,
    21	  and image checks; matching names prove nothing.
    22	- **Prime label/derivative.** A prime mark is a label unless the source defines
    23	  differentiation; rename ambiguity.
    24	- **Merge-free/M-descent.** Statement 8.5 needs each lower endpoint outside
    25	  `V_{2,a}`. A regular dirty `V_{2,a}` step can change `M` without an MP0 merge.
    26	- **Target/arrival index.** Keep fixed `nu_G` distinct from incoming `nu_U` and
    27	  legacy search indices; missing route-to-state data means fallback.
    28	
