+```text
+K3=w^3(w-1)^8
+   +sum c_(r,d) t^r (w-1)^v_r w^(d-v_r),
+v_r=max(0,ceil((33-3r)/4)),
+1<=r<=11, v_r<=d<=11-r.                                  (3.1)
+```
+
+There are exactly 21 coefficients. Substituting either minor centre into this
+same `K3` gives the computations below. In both branches the first active
+minor row contains `c_(1,8)` and forces it to zero. Hence the common jet begins
+at the first lower global `h3` coefficient, not only at a distant Jacobian
+band. Through (2.1), every `c_(r,d)` also occurs in the global `F,G`; what is
+missing from the charged local lifts is an emitted map from their independent
+local `F_n,G_n` names back to all 7161 chart coordinates.
+
+The following counts can therefore be embedded in the untouched global chart.
+After the major `h3` block, the 7161-variable chart has dimension 7116. Adding
+the minor-centre parameters and only the computed common-`h3` rows gives:
+
+| branch/stage | local `h3+centre` dimension | same stage plus 7095 untouched global variables |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| `delta=2`, before minor rows | 23 | 7118 |
+| `delta=2`, after leader | 5 | **7100** |
+| `delta=5/2`, before minor rows | 24 | 7119 |
+| `delta=5/2`, after leader | 4 | **7099** |
+| `delta=5/2`, after first ODE compatibility | 3 | **7098** |
