   360	| `delta=5/2`, after first ODE compatibility, `b0=0` | 3 | **7098** |
   361	
   362	These are exact dimensions of the displayed partial incidence schemes. They
   363	are not dimensions of `X_2` or `X_52`, because the `h2`, remaining order,
   364	minor-`F,G`, effective-root, and Jacobian rows have not yet been imposed.
   365	The last row uses the driver's `b0=0` normalization. Restoring the additive
   366	`q1` constant adds one auxiliary effective-root coordinate (local dimension 4,
   367	or 7099 with the untouched variables); it is not an extra `F,G` coefficient.
   368	
   369	The preprocessing is graded throughout. Major `h3` uses
   370	`wt(t)=3, wt(w-1)=4` with boundary 32, major `h2` uses the same weights with
   371	boundary 96, and the two minor charts are processed in increasing `t`- or
   372	`s`-exponent. The global Jacobian is to be split by the induced total/face
   373	weight before nonlinear elimination. The unrelated K=16 numerical weights
   374	were not transported into this ring.
   375	
   376	### 3.1 Projected major `h2`: exact `169 -> 162`
   377	
   378	[`major_h2_probe.py`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/major_h2_probe.py)
   379	builds the 169 strict coefficients in the invertible basis
   380	`t^r(w-1)^q`, substitutes (2.3), and extracts every scalar row below `e^296`.
   381	It finds exactly seven `Q*` pivots and no residual:
   382	
   383	| `e` power | 291 | 292 | 293 | 294 | 295 | total |
   384	|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   385	| new scalar rows/rank | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | **7** |
   386	
   387	The free dimension is 162. Every row is rechecked under the triangular map; a
   388	zero positive point passes and perturbing one pivot fails. This is
   389	`PROJECTED-MAJOR-h2-D2-D1`, not yet the nonlinear simultaneous `h3/h2` chart.
   390	
   391	### 3.2 `delta=2 [2,1]`: the common `h3` leader
   392	
   393	In (3.1) substitute `w=u*t^2+t^3*z` and require
   394	`K3=p2*t^9+O(t^10)`. Exact constant-pivot elimination gives:
   395	
   396	| minor `t` band | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 |
   397	|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   398	| new rows = rank | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 |
   399	| cumulative dimension incl. `(rho,u)` | 22 | 21 | 20 | 18 | 16 | 14 | 11 | 8 | **5** |
   400	
   401	There is no residual row and no division by `rho` or `u`. The free global
   402	`h3` coefficients are `c_(7,4),c_(10,1),c_(11,0)`. In the straight slice
   403	`u=0`, the same global polynomial gives
   404	
   405	```text
   406	W3=-8*z^4-18*rho*z^3,       W6=28*z^5+45*rho*z^4.        (3.2)
   407	```
   408	
   409	These are exactly the old-polynomial tails used by the charged branch-B lift.
   410	
   411	That separate lift uses source-ordered local polynomials
   412	`F66=G` and `G99=F` and the exact transformed Jacobian recurrence
   413	
   414	```text
   415	E_n=sum_(r+s=n)((18-s)f_r' g_s+(r-12)f_r g_s')-cJ*[n=31]. (3.3)
   416	```
   417	
   418	Its banked ledger is:
   419	
   420	| band | new unknowns | raw / quotient rows | new rank | old compatibility | dimension incl. `rho`, fixed `cJ` |
   421	|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   422	| 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 |
   423	| 1 | 43 | `32 / 27` | 26 | 0 | 18 |
   424	| 2 | 41 | `36 then 30 / 25` | 24 | 5 | 30 |
   425	| 3 | 39 | `30 / 25` | 24 | 4 | 41 |
   426	| 4 | 37 | `29 / 24` | 22 | 5 | 51 |
   427	| 5 | 35 | `28 / 23` | 22 | codimension 5 | **59** |
   428	| 6 | 33 | `27 / 22` | 20 | 17 remainder rows | **OPEN** |
