   489	
   490	## 4. Calibration controls
   491	
   492	### 4.1 Moh's `(64,48)` parent / reduced `(16,12)` kill
   493	
   494	For the `s=3,u_s=1` control, the principal-minor side is trivial: it adds zero
   495	split variables and zero split equations. Dividing the parent degrees by 4
   496	gives Moh's printed p.208 common-polynomial `(16,12)` chart. Both literal
   497	interpretations of its one typographical ambiguity were tested:
   498	
   499	* the printed repeated `c5`; and
   500	* the compiler convention absorbing `alpha1` and using a distinct `c6`.
   501	
   502	In either version there are 17 coefficient parameters plus the nonzero
   503	Jacobian scalar `kappa`, hence 18 unknowns excluding the wrapper, and 77
   504	coefficient rows. Over the declared rational polynomial ring, adjoining
   505	`T*kappa-1` gives reduced Groebner basis `[1]`. The raw ideal retains its origin
   506	at `kappa=0`, so the result is genuinely the localized component, not a raw
   507	unit ideal. Wrapper, ring, and positive/negative controls pass. Verdict:
   508	
   509	```text
   510	SATURATED-EMPTY[P208-COMMON-POLYNOMIAL-ANSATZ].
   511	```
   512	
   513	The independent charged order spine also reproduces the kill: 23 rows in 18
   514	unknowns reduce by seven `Q*` pivots to 15 rows in 11 variables; after four
   515	more affine pivots over `Q[z]/(54z^2-36z+5)`, the terminal element
   516	`20z-10/3` is a unit, with explicit identity
   517	`(20z-10/3)(27/10-27z/5)-1=-2(54z^2-36z+5)`.
   518	This is an exact characteristic-zero calibration certificate, not evidence that
   519	the uncomputed `(99,66)` ideal is empty.
   520	
   521	### 4.2 A genuine automorphism that must survive
   522	
   523	For `a!=0`, compose the two triangular affine automorphisms
   524	
   525	```text
   526	T1(x,y)=(a*x+y,y),
   527	T2(u,v)=(u,((a-1)u+v)/a).
   528	```
   529	
   530	Their determinants are `a` and `1/a`, and the composition is
   531	
   532	```text
   533	F=a*x+y,             G=(a-1)*x+y,
   534	J(F,G)=1,            x=F-G, y=aG-(a-1)F.                (4.1)
   535	```
   536	
   537	Both are monic in `y` with `deg=deg_y=1`. Their projective closures meet the
   538	line at infinity at the two distinct points
   539	`P_F=[1:-a:0]` and `P_G=[1:1-a:0]`. At these points the exact jets are
   540	`(tF,tG)=(pi,pi-1)` and `(pi+1,pi)`. In the shared ansatz
   541	`F=A*x+y,G=C*x+y`, both point charts and the direct Jacobian reduce to the same
   542	row `A-C-1`; the two-variable family has dimension one, and the slice `A=2`
   543	gives the rational witness `(2x+y,x+y)` of dimension zero.
   544	
   545	This is `EXACT-AUTOMORPHISM / SURVIVES[UNIVERSAL-GLOBAL-CHECKS]`. The special
   546	`s=3` tower and principal-minor split are
   547	`NOT-APPLICABLE[degrees (1,1)]`; the control tests only that the common-global
   548	coefficient plumbing and direct Jacobian do not falsely kill a real two-chart
   549	automorphism.
   550	
   551	## 5. Reproducibility and controls
   552	
   553	All new writes are under `box/g9966-20260903/` except this report. The main
   554	artifact manifest is
   555	[`artifacts.sha256`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/artifacts.sha256);
   556	the calibration and Xu extension have their own validated manifests.
   557	
   558	| computation | driver/result | exact outcome | replay cost |
   559	|---|---|---|---:|
   560	| common `h3`, both branches through charged cap | [`joint_probe.py`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/joint_probe.py), [`JSON`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/joint_probe-results.json) | 14/14 input hashes; all row and ring-map checks pass | 52.54 s, 69,324 KiB |
   561	| projected major `h2` | [`major_h2_probe.py`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/major_h2_probe.py), [`JSON`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/major_h2-results.json) | 7/7 pivots, dimension 162 | 0.97 s, 53,868 KiB |
   562	| direct minor raw-row count | [`minor_row_count.py`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/minor_row_count.py), [`JSON`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/minor_row_count.json) | 1,647 / 1,910 rows; no rank claim | 1.19 s, 18,528 KiB |
   563	| Xu extension | [`xu_joint_extension.py`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/xu_joint_extension/xu_joint_extension.py), [`JSON`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/xu_joint_extension/xu_joint_extension.json) | consistent through `s^28` | 191.92 s, 185,372 KiB |
   564	| calibrations | [`calibration_controls.py`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/calibration/calibration_controls.py), [`JSON`](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/g9966-20260903/calibration/calibration-results.json) | positive and negative controls pass | 20.26 s total replay |
   565	
   566	The common-jet drivers use declared polynomial/Laurent maps, deterministic
   567	rational-constant `Q*` pivots, and simultaneous substitution back into every
   568	original row. Each has a positive point and a one-pivot perturbation that is
   569	rejected. The Xu extension also rechecks all scalar coefficient rows at all 30
   570	ODE levels, not only the pivot rows. The calibration saturation asserts its result ring and
   571	separately tests empty and nonempty wrappers. The K=16 preprocessing was read
   572	for these methods but not run as `(99,66)` evidence: its tuple and ring are
   573	different, exactly as the charged audit warns at
   574	[`xu-delta52-lift...md:305`](/tmp/jc2-lane.eijAga/inputs/xu-delta52-lift-gpt55-20260903.md:305).
   575	
   576	## 6. Verdict, bounded quantity, and cheapest decisive test
   577	
   578	The principal bounded quantity is now exact:
   579	
   580	```text
   581	global fixed-top ambient                         7161 coefficients
   582	first common h3 partial family, delta=2          7100 incl. centre parameters
   583	first common h3 partial family, delta=5/2        7098 after ODE compatibility, b0=0
   584	direct Jacobian coefficient slots               <=13,366
   585	```
   586	
   587	The two large dimensions retain 7095 untouched global variables; they measure
   588	only the first common block. They are **not** evidence that the final variety
   589	is large. Conversely, consistency through band 5 or `s^28` is not attainment.
   590	
   591	For `delta=2`, the deepest complete local `F,G` band is 5 (dimension 59 in its
   592	own slice), and the next system is band 6 with 17 remainder rows. For
   593	`delta=5/2`, the deepest common-`h3` reduced ODE band is `s^28`, dimension 3 at
   594	`c=1` with `b0`, and (3.6) is the exact next system. Neither branch is
   595	inconsistent, so there is no kill certificate to present.
   596	
   597	The cheapest test with a chance to decide something genuinely new is **not**
   598	another unconstrained local prolongation. It is to serialize one common global
   599	band map from (2.1):
   600	
   601	1. finish the simultaneous `h3/h2` major fibre product through the seven
   602	   `D1` rows;
   603	2. pull the first minor `F,G` leader rows (2.4) or (2.6) back to those same
   604	   `H,C2,C3,A2,A3,B1,B2` variables; and
   605	3. add the first nonzero weighted block of the direct Jacobian, using `Q*`
   606	   pivots before any Groebner elimination.
   607	
   608	An empty localized ideal there would be a valid finite necessary-condition
   609	kill for that branch. A nonempty result would remain a counting bound, but it
   610	would identify the first actual cross-point between the two infinity charts and
   611	the Jacobian. Only after a full specialization is recomposed into polynomials
   612	and `F_xG_y-F_yG_x` is checked identically as `1` may it be called a Keller
   613	pair.
   614	
   615	FALLACY-v2 audit: no cv flag is identified with a place or cover series; no
   616	lower bound is promoted to attainment; all saturations declare their rings and
   617	controls; raw remainders are checked in their stated quotient; source and
   618	driver variable maps are typed; derivative primes occur only where declared;
   619	and every stopped lift is labeled `COUNTING-BOUND` or `OPEN`. No new exit-price
   620	assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` declaration is emitted.

