+### 2.4 Direct Jacobian and the joint schemes
+
+Let `Imaj` be all coefficient rows from section 2.1 in the 7161-variable chart,
+and let `Imin,2` and `Imin,52` be the coefficient rows (2.4) and (2.6), including
+the indicated nonzero localization. Define
+
+```text
+IJ = < [x^i y^j](F_x G_y-F_y G_x-1) : i,j>=0, i+j<=162 >,
+X_2  = Spec R_2 /(Imaj+Imin,2 +IJ),
+X_52 = Spec R_52/(Imaj+Imin,52+IJ).                       (2.8)
+```
+
+This is the base finite-support global major/minor-leader/Jacobian incidence
+construction: both local charts are images of the **same** coefficient arrays
+in (2.1), and (2.8), not a local ODE, contains the actual Jacobian equation.
+It is not yet the complete requested Moh/Xu joint system because the effective
+root bridge described below is absent. Before local-centre variables and a
+Rabinowitsch wrapper, its global ambient has exactly 7161 unknowns. Branch 2
+adds `(u,rho)` and branch 52 adds `(u,v,c)`; the torus slices remove `rho` or
+`c` respectively.
+
+The degree-163 homogeneous part of the Jacobian vanishes identically because
+the top forms are powers `P^9,P^6`. Therefore an economical direct expansion
+has at most
+
+```text
+1+2+...+163 = 13,366
+```
+
+coefficient rows in degrees 0 through 162 (the constant row has target 1).
+Further structural zeros and dependencies must be detected, not guessed. No
+rank for this block was computed.
+
+The effective `T2,T3 in k(x)[F,G]` equations and the condition excluding a
+later split inside the double packet are additional necessary derived blocks.
+Their explicit source recurrences are not among the frozen inputs: Moh says the
+radius-2 case reduces to 11 variables but does not print the variables or the
