+These are exact dimensions of the displayed partial incidence schemes. They
+are not dimensions of `X_2^FG` or `X_52^FG`, because the `h2`, remaining order,
+minor-`F,G`, effective-root, and Jacobian rows have not yet been imposed.
+The last row uses the driver's `b0=0` normalization. Restoring the additive
+`q1` constant adds one auxiliary effective-root coordinate (local dimension 4,
