+In either version there are 17 coefficient parameters plus the nonzero
+Jacobian scalar `kappa`, hence 18 unknowns excluding the wrapper, and 77
+coefficient rows. Over the declared rational polynomial ring, adjoining
+`T*kappa-1` gives reduced Groebner basis `[1]`. The raw ideal retains its origin
+at `kappa=0`, so the result is genuinely the localized component, not a raw
+unit ideal. Wrapper, ring, and positive/negative controls pass. Verdict:
