+### 2.4 Direct Jacobian and the joint schemes
+
+Let `C` be the polynomial ring over `k` in the 7161 named coordinates of
+(2.1), and declare
+
+```text
+R_2  = C[u,rho,rho^-1],              R_52=C[u,v,c,c^-1].
+```
