+Moh and Xu instead call the degree-66 polynomial `f` and the degree-99
+polynomial `g`. Thus `(F,G)=(g_Moh,f_Moh)`, and their oriented Jacobian is
+`J(G,F)=-1`. This reversal matters for the principal-minor multiplicity:
