+## 4. Calibration controls
+
+### 4.1 Moh's `(64,48)` parent / reduced `(16,12)` kill
+
+For the requested `s=3,u_s=1` control, no separate principal-minor split block
+is appended: it adds zero split variables and zero split equations. Dividing
+the parent degrees by 4 gives Moh's printed p.208 common-polynomial `(16,12)`
+chart. The literal typography and the compiler's conventional alternative were
+both tested:
+
+* the printed repeated `c5`; and
+* the compiler convention absorbing `alpha1` and using a distinct `c6`.
+
+The distinction and source text are recorded at
+[`jet-edge-1612...md:68`](/tmp/jc2-lane.eijAga/inputs/jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903.md:68);
+`OPEN[PRINTED-C5-EMENDATION]` remains for general reuse even though both tested
+control ideals are empty.
+
+In either version there are 17 coefficient parameters plus the nonzero
+Jacobian scalar `kappa`, hence 18 unknowns excluding the wrapper, and 77
+coefficient rows. Over the declared rational polynomial ring, adjoining
+`T*kappa-1` gives reduced Groebner basis `[1]`. The raw ideal retains its origin
+at `kappa=0`, so the result is genuinely the localized component, not a raw
+unit ideal. Wrapper, ring, and positive/negative controls pass. Verdict:
+
+```text
+SATURATED-EMPTY[P208-COMMON-POLYNOMIAL-ANSATZ].
+```
+
+The independent charged order spine also reproduces the kill: 23 rows in 18
+unknowns reduce by seven `Q*` pivots to 15 rows in 11 variables; after four
+more affine pivots over `Q[z]/(54z^2-36z+5)`, the terminal element
+`20z-10/3` is a unit, with explicit identity
+`(20z-10/3)(27/10-27z/5)-1=-2(54z^2-36z+5)`.
